WEBVTT

00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:19.650
We're supposed to be on winter break...

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:21.290
We worked hard again today, didn't we?

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:22.470
We did! We really did!

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:24.770
After all, we...

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:30.920
I will now announce the results of the 
Verone Academy's singing competition...

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:32.640
The winner is...

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:34.210
Second year, Sakura class.

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:38.890
On top of winning the school competition,

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:41.690
we'll be representing the 
school at the year-end

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:44.160
Seibu Regional Middle School 
Singing Competition.

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:46.380
We'd better do our best.

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:49.330
We owe it all to you don't we, Yabe-san?

00:00:49.330 --> 00:00:52.320
That's right. Your strict 
guidance out of love is

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:55.100
what brought us this far, Chiaki.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:57.950
We'll follow you anywhere!

00:00:57.950 --> 00:00:59.070
We're counting on you again this time.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:05.010
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:07.680
<i>Pretty Cure Pretty Cure</i>

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:10.450
<i>Pretty Cure Pretty Cure</i>

00:01:10.650 --> 00:01:14.920
<i>We're pretty and cure cure Together we are...</i>

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:17.620
<i>PRETTY CURE...!</i>

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:20.760
<i>Out of the frying pan, into the fire</i>

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:22.360
<i>Frankly, it's totally unbelievable</i>

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:26.360
<i>Even in our school in our 
school uniforms, we're both</i>

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:28.170
<i>amazingly tough</i>

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:33.970
<i>Each time we get out of a tight spot,</i>

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:35.940
<i>we both</i>

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:37.280
<i>become stronger</i>

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:39.840
<i>and closer</i>

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:43.850
<i>Yeah! Your best! My best! Because we're alive</i>

00:01:43.850 --> 00:01:46.420
<i>we never fail!</i>

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:49.590
<i>Don't you know that good fortune</i>

00:01:49.590 --> 00:01:52.160
<i>comes to the gates of laughter?
Out with the negative!</i>

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:58.330
<i>Brighten up your life!
Try with all your might...</i>

00:01:58.730 --> 00:01:59.630
<i>Work like the devil!</i>

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:02.100
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:05.140
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:09.410
<i>We're pretty and cure cure Together we are</i>

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:12.480
<i>Pretty Cure!</i>

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:16.210
<i>Pretty Cure! Pretty Cure!</i>

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:31.260
What was that anyway?

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:37.940
In any case, we'll just get rid of anything

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:40.300
that gets in our way, and 
just take what we need.

00:02:40.710 --> 00:02:45.560
If we do that, we'll get out from under 
the spell of the Power of Annihilation.

00:02:49.810 --> 00:02:52.380
But have we really evolved?

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:56.580
If we have, how much time do we have left?

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:58.290
We'll have to hurry.

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:00.590
We'll have to hurry.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.980
We'll have to hurry...! We'll have to hurry!

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:07.400
They're finally beginning 
to feel the pressure.

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:14.280
"SING, SAKURA CLASS! THE CHOIR SHOWS COURAGE"

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:23.060
Everyone's so enthusiastic, so we may be 
able to win this year's singing competition.

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:24.120
Don't you think so, Honoka?

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:26.550
You're right. We could.

00:03:26.550 --> 00:03:28.190
What's wrong, Honoka?

00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:29.440
Don't tell me, you're...?

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:31.420
Let's do our best during practice.

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:32.960
See you tomorrow!

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:35.640
Bye!

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:44.770
It looks like they've realized that Pollun 
holds the power of the stones inside him.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:48.740
And those warriors from Dotsuku Zone 
seem to have grown more powerful.

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:51.720
We'll have to be even 
more careful than before.

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:53.220
But...

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:56.910
That was Kiriya-kun, wasn't it?

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.800
What's going on anyway?

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:01.010
What's going to happen from here on?

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:03.570
I was surprised, too, but...

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:06.890
Honoka...?

00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:19.640
Chiaki!

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:21.900
Hey, Chiaki!

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:23.410
Nagisa?

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:26.860
A new song?

00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:30.210
What's wrong with the song we sang 
for the school singing competition?

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:33.140
I heard from one of the senior members of the

00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:35.620
music club that Otakaku 
Girls' School is going

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:39.590
to be singing a really high-level song.

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:41.470
That's awesome.

00:04:41.470 --> 00:04:43.720
We don't have time to be impressed, do we?

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:47.130
Do you want Otakaku Girls' School 
to take the championship from us?

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:48.900
You're right.

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:51.720
We might not have enough 
time even if we practice

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:53.310
a high-level song from now, but...

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:57.210
Maybe I could find a song 
that's easy, but has impact...

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:59.060
We might be able to beat Otakaku.

00:04:59.380 --> 00:05:01.470
In that case, we should look over here...

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:11.490
This isn't it.

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:17.920
This isn't it either.

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:21.630
What is it? Did you find a good song?

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:30.580
Nagisa!

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:36.780
This is no good either.

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:39.750
I guess it's too late to find one now.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:43.720
I thought it was a good idea.

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:54.070
Chiaki! How's this one, Chiaki?

00:05:58.810 --> 00:06:00.040
This is good.

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:01.930
Isn't it? Isn't it?

00:06:07.330 --> 00:06:10.640
So we're going to change our song.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:12.030
You're kidding! You must be kidding!

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:14.220
Are we going to practice a new song from now?

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:16.370
Isn't it too late?

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:19.790
That means what we practiced until yesterday 
will all be for nothing now, won't it?

00:06:20.090 --> 00:06:24.200
I just got to the point where I have 
confidence in playing the piano accompaniment.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:26.040
We have to do it now.

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:28.360
I understand what you're 
all saying, but unless

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:32.670
we sing a long like this one, we 
won't be able to win against Otakaku.

00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:36.640
It's not your ordinary song for a choir...

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:43.700
I don't know if it's a good song for a choir,

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:45.700
but I think it's a song people will get into.

00:06:47.330 --> 00:06:49.750
In any case, let's listen to it once.

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:32.230
I tried to arrange it for a choir, so if

00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:35.100
there's any part that's 
hard to play, tell me.

00:07:36.190 --> 00:07:38.570
This doesn't look too hard to do.

00:07:39.410 --> 00:07:40.660
Let me try it.

00:07:52.010 --> 00:07:53.550
That's pretty good.

00:08:13.960 --> 00:08:16.860
I'll practice this at home, 
so I'll be able to play

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:18.640
it perfectly by the end of today.

00:08:21.630 --> 00:08:22.690
Isn't that great?

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:24.020
Everyone's really enthusiastic.

00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:28.110
Something's missing.

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:28.890
Chiaki?

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:31.530
It needs something more.

00:08:32.060 --> 00:08:33.800
I wonder what's wrong with Chiaki?

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:50.950
You've learned the whole song, haven't you?

00:08:50.950 --> 00:08:53.110
It's so much fun to sing mipo.

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:56.440
For two lovebirds like us...

00:08:56.440 --> 00:08:58.110
A love song is...

00:08:58.110 --> 00:08:59.880
-Perfect for us mepo!

00:08:58.110 --> 00:08:59.880
-Perfect for us mipo!

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:02.590
That's not fair popo!

00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:04.980
How could you leave me out like this!

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:06.610
It's not fair.... Not fair popo!

00:09:06.610 --> 00:09:08.270
It's not fair popo!

00:09:08.270 --> 00:09:11.330
Don't make such a big fuss!

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:15.630
I wonder if Yabe-san will be okay...

00:09:16.590 --> 00:09:18.940
That's right... Chiaki's 
the type to put her heart

00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:20.620
and soul into whatever she does...

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:25.580
That's why she's brought 
all of us this far, but...

00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:42.860
The harmony of the altos and 
sopranos is perfect, but

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:45.330
there's something missing.

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:52.570
What could it be?

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:08.260
Chiaki's late...

00:10:08.720 --> 00:10:11.290
She's never been late to practice before.

00:10:20.490 --> 00:10:23.220
No one answers at Yabe-san's house,

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:25.000
so I think she's heading over here.

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:26.620
It can't be helped...

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:28.870
Shall we just start practicing then?

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:09.600
What's Chiaki doing anyway?

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:11.780
She hasn't come to practice for three days...

00:11:12.130 --> 00:11:14.630
The competition is coming up soon...
 What is she planning to do?

00:11:14.630 --> 00:11:16.130
If she changes the arrangement, I might

00:11:16.130 --> 00:11:17.590
be able to play it the way she wants.

00:11:17.590 --> 00:11:19.340
That's true... That's so true...

00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:22.060
I'm beginning to lose the will to do this.

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:24.530
Me, too!

00:11:24.530 --> 00:11:28.220
Not showing up at all is bad, isn't it?

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:30.440
But without Yabe-san...

00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:32.300
No! That's no good...

00:11:32.730 --> 00:11:34.740
Sopranos... don't come on too strong there...

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:37.630
And altos... try to come in on time.

00:11:40.160 --> 00:11:44.280
Without Chiaki, we wouldn't have been 
chosen to represent the school, would we?

00:11:45.300 --> 00:11:48.220
Yabe-san was strict with us, 
but more than anyone else,

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:50.620
she was hardest on herself.

00:11:50.620 --> 00:11:52.630
That's why I think she's 
trying her best on her own.

00:11:52.630 --> 00:11:53.560
That may be true.

00:11:56.700 --> 00:11:59.880
It's up to all of you if you'll have faith in

00:11:59.880 --> 00:12:01.300
Yabe-san and stick with her until the end.

00:12:01.560 --> 00:12:02.770
Ms. Yoshimi!

00:12:02.980 --> 00:12:04.900
I brought you "takoyaki" (octopus dumplings).

00:12:10.600 --> 00:12:13.640
I'm sorry. I'm just totally stuck on this.

00:12:13.640 --> 00:12:16.420
That's okay... Relax. Just relax.

00:12:16.770 --> 00:12:19.280
In any case, everyone's working hard to get

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:22.840
their parts down perfectly 
until you come back.

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:23.720
Really?

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:27.590
"So why am I stuffing my face 
with chocolates like this?"

00:12:27.590 --> 00:12:30.400
Everyone really gets into this 
part, so it's going just perfectly.

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:35.010
"I'm a teenager..."

00:12:35.010 --> 00:12:37.630
"with a heart-throbbing exciting dream..."

00:12:38.050 --> 00:12:44.630
"I don't want to lose that 
normal everyday routine..."

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:45.720
That's it!

00:12:46.330 --> 00:12:47.710
We needed a solo part.

00:12:58.070 --> 00:12:59.060
This is the solo part.

00:12:59.340 --> 00:13:05.760
"I'm a teenager with a 
heart-throbbing exciting dream."

00:13:06.270 --> 00:13:12.700
"I don't want to lose that 
normal everyday routine."

00:13:13.250 --> 00:13:19.680
"I just can't do this! It's romance 
rather than stress, isn't it?"

00:13:19.680 --> 00:13:22.250
"Get you! Into a love love mode."

00:13:22.250 --> 00:13:26.000
"Isn't that the best source of power?"

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:28.010
"I just can't so this..."

00:13:32.640 --> 00:13:34.160
It's awesome... Really awesome!

00:13:34.630 --> 00:13:37.500
The solo really made it better than it was.

00:13:37.500 --> 00:13:38.920
We knew you could do it, Chiaki.

00:13:40.060 --> 00:13:42.270
But letting us do a solo...

00:13:42.270 --> 00:13:43.840
To be honest, it's totally unbelievable.

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:44.940
Don't worry...

00:13:44.940 --> 00:13:46.770
I'll give you extra special training.

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:03.920
He's fast asleep.

00:14:03.920 --> 00:14:06.140
Let him sleep until the competition is over.

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:08.460
I'm so nervous.

00:14:09.940 --> 00:14:11.520
Relax... just relax.

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:13.230
You're right.

00:14:14.990 --> 00:14:16.970
I'm counting on the two of you.

00:14:16.970 --> 00:14:18.640
Let's do our best, Nagisa.

00:14:18.640 --> 00:14:20.300
Let's go and wash our face to calm us down.

00:14:37.840 --> 00:14:44.080
The 25th annual Seibu Regional Middle School 
Singing Competition will now begin...

00:14:46.130 --> 00:14:47.030
We can't find Nagisa...

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:48.370
Or Honoka anywhere.

00:14:48.630 --> 00:14:49.880
Did you look everywhere?

00:14:49.880 --> 00:14:52.890
Of course! We looked in the bathroom, 
lobby and even in the audience...

00:14:52.890 --> 00:14:54.970
Everywhere! We looked everywhere!

00:14:55.320 --> 00:14:57.540
Where did those two go?

00:14:57.540 --> 00:14:59.600
The might not make it back in time.

00:15:02.790 --> 00:15:03.620
Nagisa...

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:07.340
Honoka! Don't scare me like that!

00:15:15.280 --> 00:15:16.930
Nagisa... be careful mepo!

00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:19.630
I feel a really evil presence mipo!

00:15:19.990 --> 00:15:21.230
I know...!

00:15:27.100 --> 00:15:28.870
-There he is mepo!

00:15:27.100 --> 00:15:28.870
-There he is mipo!

00:15:35.070 --> 00:15:37.950
Today is our important competition...

00:15:37.950 --> 00:15:39.920
We won't let you get in our way!

00:15:44.940 --> 00:15:47.670
Dual Aurora Wave!

00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:16.690
Protector of the Light, Cure Black!

00:16:17.040 --> 00:16:19.290
Protector of the Light, Cure White!

00:16:21.560 --> 00:16:22.810
Together, we're Pretty Cure!

00:16:24.440 --> 00:16:26.430
Servants of the power of darkness...

00:16:27.410 --> 00:16:29.870
Go back to where you came from!

00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:45.620
It's too... too sudden for us to do the solo!

00:16:46.090 --> 00:16:47.620
To be honest... it's totally unbelievable.

00:17:17.890 --> 00:17:19.380
I've had enough of this already!

00:17:19.620 --> 00:17:21.460
We don't have time for this!

00:17:24.000 --> 00:17:26.420
We don't have time either.

00:17:43.010 --> 00:17:43.830
Popo...

00:17:45.020 --> 00:17:46.280
Nagisa... Honoka...?

00:18:01.380 --> 00:18:03.090
Do your best, everybody.

00:18:03.530 --> 00:18:05.950
Isn't it time you gave up?

00:18:06.430 --> 00:18:09.230
Do you think we'd do that?

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:11.900
You people might not understand, but...

00:18:11.900 --> 00:18:14.210
What's important to us is...

00:18:15.140 --> 00:18:16.970
To laugh and cry with everyone...

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:19.740
All the things a normal girl would do.

00:18:20.940 --> 00:18:23.050
Do you think we'll stand for anyone 
who would interfere with that?

00:18:23.050 --> 00:18:26.170
Then don't get in our way!

00:18:33.980 --> 00:18:37.170
They're both in danger popo!

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:52.270
Accept the power of light popo!

00:19:10.140 --> 00:19:10.860
What...?

00:19:37.980 --> 00:19:40.630
Power of hope... Take the will of light...

00:19:41.480 --> 00:19:44.100
And fight your way toward the future!

00:19:44.600 --> 00:19:47.740
Pretty Cure Rainbow Storm!

00:21:07.190 --> 00:21:13.580
I'm a teenager with a 
heart-throbbing exciting dream

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:20.870
"I don't want to lose that 
normal everyday routine"

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:27.600
"I just can't do this! It's romance 
rather than stress, isn't it?"

00:21:27.600 --> 00:21:30.130
"Get you! Into a love love mode."

00:21:30.130 --> 00:21:33.890
"Isn't that the best source of power?"

00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:37.140
"I just can't do this!"

00:21:37.140 --> 00:21:40.380
"I'd rather cuddle than fight and..."

00:21:40.380 --> 00:21:42.980
"Get you! Into a love love mode"

00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:45.620
"That's the most peaceful way"

00:21:45.620 --> 00:21:47.170
"So why am I"

00:21:47.170 --> 00:21:48.780
"stuffing my face"

00:21:48.780 --> 00:21:52.210
"with chocolates like this?"

00:22:04.090 --> 00:22:05.520
You all hung in there, didn't you?

00:22:06.050 --> 00:22:07.850
The Sakura class is the greatest.

00:22:07.850 --> 00:22:09.330
Thank you, everybody.

00:22:10.240 --> 00:22:11.280
Thank you!

00:22:24.760 --> 00:22:25.320
<i>Let's go!</i>

00:22:26.160 --> 00:22:26.860
<i>Get you!</i>

00:22:26.860 --> 00:22:29.560
<i>L-O-V-E Love Love, get you!</i>

00:22:29.660 --> 00:22:32.300
<i>I can't do this!</i>

00:22:32.530 --> 00:22:35.570
<i>I'd rather be a young lady than a fighter and</i>

00:22:35.570 --> 00:22:38.000
<i>Get you! Into a love love mode</i>

00:22:38.100 --> 00:22:42.140
<i>And melt your body and soul into sweets</i>

00:22:44.680 --> 00:22:47.850
<i>like chocolate parfait or handsome men</i>

00:22:47.910 --> 00:22:51.580
<i>I'm at the age to seriously 
fall head over heels in love</i>

00:22:52.250 --> 00:22:55.320
<i>I wanted to confess my love again today</i>

00:22:56.450 --> 00:22:59.690
<i>For the sake of the earth 
For the sake of everyone</i>

00:22:59.820 --> 00:23:06.330
<i>That's good, too, but haven't 
you forgotten something?</i>

00:23:07.430 --> 00:23:10.700
<i>I'm a teenager with a</i>

00:23:10.700 --> 00:23:13.940
<i>heart throbbing exciting dream</i>

00:23:13.940 --> 00:23:16.670
<i>I don't want to lose that</i>

00:23:16.670 --> 00:23:20.450
<i>normal everyday routine</i>

00:23:20.450 --> 00:23:22.950
<i>I just can't do this!</i>

00:23:23.180 --> 00:23:26.420
<i>It's romance rather than stress, isn't it?</i>

00:23:26.420 --> 00:23:28.590
<i>Get you! Into a love love mode</i>

00:23:28.590 --> 00:23:31.890
<i>Isn't that the best source of power?</i>

00:23:32.190 --> 00:23:34.930
<i>I just can't do this!</i>

00:23:35.390 --> 00:23:38.200
<i>I'd rather cuddle than fight and...</i>

00:23:38.200 --> 00:23:40.430
<i>Get you! Into a love love mode</i>

00:23:40.430 --> 00:23:42.970
<i>That's the most peaceful way</i>

00:23:43.100 --> 00:23:44.370
<i>So why am I</i>

00:23:44.500 --> 00:23:45.970
<i>stuffing my face</i>

00:23:46.040 --> 00:23:49.670
<i>with chocolates like this?</i>

00:23:53.980 --> 00:23:55.350
The third term will be starting soon.

00:23:55.350 --> 00:23:57.070
Our second year is almost over.

00:23:57.070 --> 00:23:59.210
It went by quickly, didn't it?

00:23:59.210 --> 00:24:00.820
So many things happened...

00:24:00.820 --> 00:24:03.000
Mepple and Mipple... And Pollun, too.

00:24:03.260 --> 00:24:04.030
Pollun?

00:24:04.890 --> 00:24:06.820
Nagisa! The dark warriors have Pollun...!

00:24:06.820 --> 00:24:09.310
What are they trying to do, Honoka?

00:24:09.310 --> 00:24:12.180
Is that a spell to draw out 
the power of the Prism Stones?

00:24:12.880 --> 00:24:16.570
"IT'S THE PITS! HAS THE POWER 
OF THE STONES BEEN STOLEN?!"

00:24:16.570 --> 00:24:18.890
We'll save you, Pollun.

00:24:18.890 --> 00:24:19.800
So hang in there.
